#4200
The Main Deck of the Sea Wren~
   The broad, scrubbed deck of the Sea Wren, a fat-bellied coastal trader
with two masts and patched brown sails.  Coils of rope, water casks and
lashed crates crowd the rails, and the deck rises and falls under your
feet.  The forecastle is forward to the north and the quarterdeck aft to
the south.  A hatch leads down below decks, and the rigging climbs up
into the sails.  When the ship is in port, a gangplank runs down from the
rail on the west side.
