bell~
A brass bell, green with salt.  It is rung every half hour of the watch,
and like mad when pirates are sighted.
~
E
figurehead wren~
A carved wren, painted brown and cream, beak up into the wind.  Sailors
touch it for luck as they pass.
~
S
#4202
The Quarterdeck~
   The raised deck at the stern, where the ship is steered.  A great
spoked wheel stands before the binnacle, and a chart table is bolted to
the deck under a canvas hood.  From here the captain can see the whole
ship and a long way out to sea.  The main deck is forward.
~
