E
chart table charts~
A sea chart of the coast, weighted down with a dagger: Gnishmire, the
coral shore of Llyndyr, the long run round the eastern cape, Vice Island,
Karras and the mouth of the Widmans.  Off the cape someone has drawn a
little skull and crossbones in red ink, and written BLACKWAKE beside it.
~
E
wheel binnacle~
The ship's wheel, its spokes polished by forty years of hands.  The
compass in the binnacle swings lazily.
~
S
#4203
Up the Rigging~
   You cling to the ratlines high above the deck, with the sails cracking
and bellying around you and the whole ship swinging beneath like a
pendulum.  A small barrel of a crow's nest is lashed to the mast just
above.  From here you can see for miles.  The deck is a long way down.
~
