#4204
The Passenger Cabin~
   A low cabin under the main deck, lit by a swinging lantern.  Bunks are
built two high into the curved walls, each with a canvas curtain, and
passengers' bags are stowed under them.  It smells of tar, wet wool and
seasickness.  A ladder climbs to the hatch above, a narrow door leads aft
to the galley, and another hatch goes down into the hold.
~
